# Professional Next.js Site Template - Cursor AI Rules

## Purpose
This template adds professional components to any Next.js application, including:
- Professional Footer with MelodyWebPages branding and rotating orange G clef icon
- Google Analytics & Google Ads integration
- Cookie consent banner
- Legal pages (Privacy Policy, Terms of Service, Contact, Report Bug)
- Google Cloud deployment configuration
- Production-ready setup

## Implementation Instructions for Cursor AI

### STEP 1: Analyze Current Application
Before implementing, analyze the existing app to understand:
1. **App Name & Purpose**: Read package.json, main page content, and existing metadata
2. **Tech Stack**: Confirm Next.js version, TypeScript/JavaScript, styling approach
3. **File Structure**: Identify where components, pages, and config files are located
4. **Existing Components**: Check if Footer, Analytics, or similar components already exist

### STEP 2: Install Dependencies (if needed)
Check package.json and ensure these dependencies exist:
- axios (for API calls if needed)
- react, react-dom, next
- TypeScript types if using TypeScript

### STEP 3: Create Components Directory
If not exists, create `/components` directory at project root.

### STEP 4: Add Professional Footer Component
Create `/components/Footer.tsx` with MelodyWebPages branding:

**Key Requirements:**
- Must have 3-column grid (About, Legal, Support)
- About section: Customize description based on app's actual functionality
- Legal section: Links to /privacy-policy, /terms-of-service, /contact
- Support section: Email support, Report bug link
- Bottom section: Copyright with current year, "Created with love by MelodyWebPages"
- CRITICAL: Include rotating orange G clef icon (𝄞) with 3D animation
- Animation: 4-second 3D rotation with orange color (#f97316) and drop shadow
- Style: Modern, dark background (bg-gray-900), clean typography

**Animation Styles (MUST INCLUDE):**
```css
@keyframes rotate3d {
  0% { transform: perspective(500px) rotateY(0deg); }
  100% { transform: perspective(500px) rotateY(360deg); }
}
.gclef-3d {
  animation: rotate3d 4s linear infinite;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;
  filter: drop-shadow(0 3px 6px rgba(249, 115, 22, 0.6));
  display: inline-block;
}
```

### STEP 5: Add Google Analytics Component
Create `/components/GoogleAnalytics.tsx`:
- Uses Next.js Script component
- Reads NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID from environment
- Returns null if no ID configured
- Includes gtag initialization with proper config

### STEP 6: Add Google AdSense Component
Create `/components/GoogleAdsense.tsx`:
- Uses Next.js Script component
- Reads NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_CLIENT_ID from environment
- Returns null if no ID configured
- Uses useEffect to push ads after mount

### STEP 7: Add Cookie Consent Component
Create `/components/CookieConsent.tsx`:
- Shows banner after 1 second delay
- Stores consent in localStorage
- Accept/Decline buttons
- Link to privacy policy
- Dark bottom banner with blue accent
- Only shows if user hasn't consented

### STEP 8: Update Root Layout
Modify `app/layout.tsx`:
1. Import all new components: Footer, CookieConsent, GoogleAnalytics, GoogleAdsense
2. Add GoogleAnalytics and GoogleAdsense in <head>
3. Add {children} and Footer in <body>
4. Add CookieConsent after Footer
5. Update metadata object with app-specific details:
   - title: Based on app functionality
   - description: Comprehensive, SEO-friendly (150-160 chars)
   - keywords: Relevant to app functionality
   - authors, creator, publisher
   - openGraph and twitter metadata
   - robots: 'index, follow'

### STEP 9: Create Legal Pages
Create these pages in `app/` directory:

**app/privacy-policy/page.tsx**
- Comprehensive privacy policy
- Sections: Information Collection, Usage, Cookies, Analytics, Google Ads, User Rights, Security, Changes
- Customize based on what data the app actually collects
- Use modern card design with gradient background
- Include "Back to [App Name]" link

**app/terms-of-service/page.tsx**
- Comprehensive terms of service
- Sections: Acceptance, Service Description, Use License, User Content, IP, Third-Party Services, Disclaimers, Liability, Indemnification, Privacy, Modifications, Governing Law, Contact
- Customize service description based on actual app functionality
- Match styling with privacy policy

**app/contact/page.tsx**
- Contact information
- FAQ section (customize based on app)
- Email: melodywebpages@gmail.com
- Response time info
- Contact form (optional)

**app/report-bug/page.tsx**
- Bug report form or instructions
- Email for bug reports
- Template for what info to include
- Acknowledge response timeframe

### STEP 10: Create Environment Variables Template
Create `.env.example`:
```
# Google Analytics
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX

# Google AdSense
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_CLIENT_ID=ca-pub-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
```

Add to `.env.local` for development (DO NOT commit).

### STEP 11: Create/Update Deployment Files

**Dockerfile**
- Multi-stage build (base, deps, builder, runner)
- Node 18 alpine
- Production optimized
- Port 8080 for Cloud Run
- Non-root user for security

**cloudbuild.yaml**
- Google Cloud Build configuration
- Docker build and push to GCR
- Deploy to Cloud Run
- Region: us-central1
- Memory: 512Mi, CPU: 1
- Max instances: 10
- Allow unauthenticated (for public sites)

**next.config.js**
- Add standalone output for Docker: `output: 'standalone'`

### STEP 12: Create Supporting Files

**public/robots.txt**
```
User-agent: *
Allow: /
Sitemap: https://[your-domain.com]/sitemap.xml
```

**public/ads.txt** (if using Google AdSense)
```
google.com, pub-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX, DIRECT, f08c47fec0942fa0
```

**app/sitemap.ts** (if not exists)
- Generate sitemap with all routes
- Include homepage, legal pages, main features

### STEP 13: Update Package.json Scripts
Add/ensure these scripts exist:
```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "dev": "next dev",
    "build": "next build",
    "start": "next start -p 8080",
    "lint": "next lint",
    "docker:build": "docker build -t [app-name] .",
    "docker:run": "docker run -p 8080:8080 [app-name]"
  }
}
```

## Customization Rules

### Text Adaptation
When implementing, Cursor AI MUST:
1. **Read the app carefully** to understand its purpose
2. **Replace ALL placeholder text** with app-specific content:
   - "[App Name]" → Actual app name from package.json or main page
   - Service descriptions → Based on what app actually does
   - Feature lists → Actual features the app provides
   - FAQ items → Relevant to the specific app

### Brand Consistency
- App name/branding: Use throughout all pages
- Footer "About" section: Describe the actual app, not generic text
- Legal pages: Reference actual app name and functionality
- Metadata: Accurate titles, descriptions, keywords for SEO

### Styling Consistency
- Use Tailwind CSS (ensure it's configured)
- Color scheme: 
  - Primary: Blue (#3B82F6, #2563EB)
  - Accent: Orange (#F97316) for G clef only
  - Background: Gray-50/Gray-900 for light/dark
  - Cards: White with subtle shadows
- Typography: System fonts, clear hierarchy
- Gradients: from-blue-50 via-white to-purple-50 for page backgrounds

### Professional Standards
- All text must be grammatically correct
- No lorem ipsum or placeholder content
- Proper error handling in components
- Loading states where applicable
- Responsive design (mobile-first)
- Accessibility considerations (aria-labels, semantic HTML)

## Quality Checklist

Before completing implementation, verify:
- [ ] Footer appears on all pages with MelodyWebPages branding
- [ ] Orange rotating G clef icon animates smoothly
- [ ] All legal pages created with app-specific content
- [ ] Google Analytics component added to layout
- [ ] Google AdSense component added to layout
- [ ] Cookie consent banner appears and stores preference
- [ ] Environment variables documented in .env.example
- [ ] Dockerfile and cloudbuild.yaml created
- [ ] All links work (no 404s)
- [ ] Responsive on mobile, tablet, desktop
- [ ] No console errors or warnings
- [ ] Build succeeds (`npm run build`)
- [ ] App-specific text used throughout (no generic placeholders)

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

1. **Don't use generic text**: Always customize based on actual app
2. **Don't skip the G clef animation**: It's a signature branding element
3. **Don't forget environment variables**: Document them clearly
4. **Don't copy-paste email addresses incorrectly**: Use melodywebpages@gmail.com
5. **Don't miss the color scheme**: Orange (#F97316) only for G clef, blue for primary actions
6. **Don't forget dark mode support**: Many components support it
7. **Don't hardcode dates**: Use `new Date().getFullYear()` for copyright
8. **Don't skip the "Back to..." links**: All legal pages need navigation back

## File Structure After Implementation

```
project/
├── app/
│   ├── layout.tsx (updated)
│   ├── page.tsx (existing)
│   ├── globals.css (existing)
│   ├── privacy-policy/
│   │   └── page.tsx (new)
│   ├── terms-of-service/
│   │   └── page.tsx (new)
│   ├── contact/
│   │   └── page.tsx (new)
│   ├── report-bug/
│   │   └── page.tsx (new)
│   └── sitemap.ts (new or updated)
├── components/
│   ├── Footer.tsx (new)
│   ├── GoogleAnalytics.tsx (new)
│   ├── GoogleAdsense.tsx (new)
│   └── CookieConsent.tsx (new)
├── public/
│   ├── robots.txt (new)
│   └── ads.txt (new, if using AdSense)
├── Dockerfile (new)
